 "statement": "the l_eval records (v5) store per stencil point the pressure argument ranges and exp/trig argument counts (not the parameter values themselves; the qualifier records store the hex values); the records share case, column, steps, base state and scientific sources, so the stencil points are the same by construction, and the identical argument ranges and counts at every point confirm it. Identical (c_l, omega) at every stencil point and identical pressure argument ranges in every record: the double-double elementary-function call sites (trig in twist and kernel tables, exp in K1/K2, wr, moment, sfac) depend on (c_l, omega) only, so the three references evaluate them at the same arguments; one elementary-function qualification of the set covers the three rows. J_c's recomputed closure target evaluates float64 closure ingredients: under the scope rule of 09:44:46Z only groups that fail the registered comparison decide the double-double scope, and the closure group passes the registered comparison, so the closure ingredients stay float64 (the screen l_scope.json records them above the closure-group limit, V324) and the closure group is judged again under (l), where it passes; they do not enter the far-anchor rows."
